# Plan location and structure (EventPrism)

Do not put harness files in this package. Use:

`~/.cursor/harness/event-prism/plans/{item}.md`  
`~/.cursor/harness/event-prism/reports/{item}.md`

`{item}` is one work unit. Later tweaks to the same feature **update that file**. Do not add `plans/` or `reports/` under the repo root.

When writing or revising a harness plan, include a **Flow graph** section (mermaid). Do not leave the plan as prose + a node table only.

- Show how the **client** (app composition root, feature module, CLI, or user) talks to the package or system under change.
- Cover boot/wiring and the primary runtime call. Add skip, drop, or error edges that change behavior.
- For UI work, add a screen/route graph: where the user starts, what they tap, where they land.
- Prefer `sequenceDiagram` for call order and `flowchart` for branching. Keep node labels short.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Feature
  participant Package
  Feature->>Package: track(name, properties)
  Package-->>Feature: return immediately
```
